  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Breaking Cancer (enemy) weakpoint panels is the primary damage mechanic—hitting exposed weakpoints deals 200% bonus damage versus attacking non-weakpoint areas.",
      "Seraph (special unit) burst timing is gated by SP gauge—spend SP on Guard actions to absorb damage and build the gauge, then activate Burst at 100 SP for maximum damage windows.",
      "The 7-character party structure (3 front, 3 back, 1 support) allows full party rotation—never let front units reach critical HP; swap to fresh back-row units proactively to maintain consistent output.",
      "Gacha SSR units are tier-differentiated primarily by their Limit Break bonuses—two copies of the same SSR provide significantly more power than the base single copy.",
      "Story content provides the majority of Crystals (premium currency) through first-clear rewards—complete all story chapters before spending Crystals on gacha to maximise available pulls."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "キャンサー（敵）の弱点パネルの破壊が主要なダメージメカニック。露出した弱点へのヒットは非弱点エリアへの攻撃の200%ボーナスダメージを与える。",
      "セラフ（特殊ユニット）のバーストタイミングはSPゲージでゲートされる。ガードアクションでSPを使ってダメージを吸収しゲージを構築し、最大ダメージウィンドウのためにSP100でバーストを発動する。",
      "7キャラクターパーティ構造（前衛3、後衛3、サポート1）は完全なパーティローテーションを可能にする。前衛ユニットがクリティカルHPに達する前にスワップ。一貫した出力を維持するために後衛ユニットに先手を打って交代する。",
      "ガチャSSRユニットは主に限界突破ボーナスでティアが差別化される。同じSSRの2コピーはベースの単一コピーより大幅に多くのパワーを提供する。",
      "ストーリーコンテンツは初回クリア報酬を通じてクリスタル（プレミアム通貨）の大部分を提供する。利用可能な引きを最大化するためにガチャにクリスタルを使う前に全てのストーリー章を完了する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Unit Composition Basics",
        "body": "Build your front row with one Tank (absorbs damage, high HP), one Healer (sustains the tank), and one primary DPS. The back row mirrors this composition with a secondary DPS, a utility unit (debuffer or buffer), and a second healer. Unlike most RPGs, Heaven Burns Red's back-row units recover HP passively while in reserve—use this mechanic to cycle damaged units out of the front row for recovery rather than using heal items."
      },
      {
        "title": "Cancer Fight Fundamentals",
        "body": "Each Cancer enemy displays a HP bar with labelled weakpoint panels. Hitting a panel with matching elemental damage breaks it—broken panels expose the Cancer's core for 2 turns of unreduced damage. Coordinate break attempts so multiple characters hit the same panel in the same turn; hitting the same panel from different characters simultaneously in one turn guarantees a break. Panels regenerate after the exposure window closes; plan your break cycles around the panel regeneration timer."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Tower of Heaven Event Strategy",
        "body": "Tower of Heaven events are limited-time vertical dungeon challenges that provide the highest-value event rewards. Tower floors become progressively harder with unique modifier rules per floor. Maintain a second party composition specifically for Tower events—tower modifiers often restrict specific unit types that your main party relies on. The critical Tower mechanic: floor bosses have specific weakpoint configurations that require element diversity; bring at least 3 different elemental attackers."
      },
      {
        "title": "Limit Break and Potential System",
        "body": "Limit Breaking SSR characters (via duplicate copies) unlocks unique passive skills and stat boosts unavailable through normal levelling. A single Limit Break (2nd copy) provides approximately 15% DPS increase on average. The Potential system (equipping Potential chips) adds targeted stat bonuses—prioritise Potential chips with ATK+ and HP+ on front-row DPS units, and Recovery Rate+ on healer units for maximum team synergy."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Extreme Raid and Gauntlet Modes",
        "body": "Extreme difficulty raids feature multi-phase bosses with phase-specific weakpoint configurations. The most consistent endgame strategy: identify the Cancer's phase transition trigger (usually breaking the main core weakpoint) and prepare burst damage immediately before triggering the transition—the 2-turn exposure window from core break aligns perfectly with Seraph burst activation, creating the highest possible burst damage window. Gauntlet modes require 0-item clears; build teams specifically for sustain over damage output in Gauntlet."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Using Seraph Burst before breaking weakpoints—Burst windows are most valuable during core-exposed phases; activating Burst on unbroken enemies wastes the highest damage amplification on armoured targets.",
      "Ignoring SP generation from Guard actions—Guard action is not just damage reduction; it also generates SP faster than attacking in most scenarios, making Guard the primary SP generation tool for Seraph timing.",
      "Not rotating back-row units for HP recovery—Heaven Burns Red's passive back-row HP regeneration is the primary healing mechanic; players who never swap units must rely on item healing, which is limited per battle.",
      "Pulling gacha without targeting event-limited characters—standard gacha characters are available permanently; event-limited characters (often stronger and story-relevant) disappear after the event period without reruns.",
      "Missing daily missions for Crystal income—daily missions provide 30–50 Crystals per day; over a month this accumulates to a significant pull count that single-session players who ignore dailies permanently miss."
    ],
